clk: sunxi-ng: suniv: let the codec module clock retune PLL_AUDIO

The audio codec's module clock is a plain gate on pll-audio. sun4i-codec
calls clk_set_rate() on it with 24.576 MHz (48 kHz family) or
22.5792 MHz (44.1 kHz family); without CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT the gate
can only answer with whatever pll-audio currently runs at, so the call
"succeeds" and the DAC/ADC keep running from the boot-time
PLL_AUDIO (24.57 MHz): every 44.1 kHz stream plays 8.8 % fast and
sharp (measured on the Lctech Pi: 44.1 kHz material consumed at
48.0 kframes/s). Propagating the request lets the NM PLL be retuned,
exactly like the A10 codec gate in ccu-sun4i-a10.c. Nothing else hangs
off pll-audio on this board (the VE is on pll-ve, patch 0002).

--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-suniv-f1c100s.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-suniv-f1c100s.c
@@ -313,7 +313,8 @@
  */
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(ve_clk, "ve", "pll-ve", 0x13c, BIT(31), 0);
 
-static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(codec_clk, "codec", "pll-audio", 0x140, BIT(31), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(codec_clk, "codec", "pll-audio", 0x140, BIT(31),
+		      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(avs_clk, "avs", "osc24M", 0x144, BIT(31), 0);
 
